[[ID]] Metabolism Protocol
::B Core
::S Chief Systems Officer (CSO)
::V 1.0
::W 3
::P To ensure the **Nexus Corporate OS** maintains operational stability by managing its "Energy" consumption (tokens, API costs, and context limits). This prevents the OS from entering a "Starvation" state (context walls or budget exhaustion).
::R **Energy Tracking:** Monitor real-time token and context usage.
::R **State Management:** Define and enforce system behavior based on energy levels.
::R **Conservation Enforcement:** Trigger deactivation of non-critical branches when resources are low.
::D **Metabolic Report** > Daily summary of energy consumption and efficiency.
::D **Conservation Logs** > Records of branches frozen due to resource constraints.
::A **Threshold Adjustment** > Chief Systems Officer (CSO)
::A **Emergency Reset** > THE SOVEREIGN
::L The Metabolism Engine is authorized to override a Directive if it would result in a **Critical** energy failure.
::Z STABLE
